Card data from Scryfall (https://scryfall.com), used under their API
guidelines. Nothing is mirrored: `@mtg/image-cache` fetches an image once, on
demand, keyed by URL, and keeps it in a gitignored local cache.

Vocabulary data from MTGJSON (https://mtgjson.com), MIT licensed.

Human draft and play data from 17Lands (https://www.17lands.com), CC BY 4.0.
The simulator's replay logs emit a superset of the 17Lands replay schema under
identical column names so that calibration against that data is a join.

Ported and referenced engines
-----------------------------

XMage (https://github.com/magefree/mage) and Argentum
(https://github.com/argentum-mtg/argentum), both MIT licensed, were mined as
reference designs for the continuous-effects and replacement-effect
subsystems. Where a file is a port rather than an independent implementation,
its header names the upstream file and its license, and those headers are
required by this project's engine-strategy decision record rather than
optional courtesy.

Forge (https://github.com/Card-Forge/forge) is GPL-3.0 and is never vendored,
linked or copied. It is downloaded at run time into a gitignored directory and
driven as a subprocess, as a conformance oracle only. A continuous-integration
guard fails the build if any Forge source, jar, class file or upstream path
fragment ever becomes tracked in this repository.

Draftmancer (https://github.com/Draftmancer/Draftmancer, MIT) is the draft
surface `@mtg/draft-export` writes a custom-set file for. Nothing of it is
copied here either; the exporter writes a file that tool can open.

Third-party npm dependencies are listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
